360,"elapsed":107287,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"}},"outputId":"cabef554-2099-43e3-d479-850346163e49"},"execution_count":2,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Mounted at /content/drive\n","Google Drive mounted successfully.\n","Data loaded successfully from Google Drive.\n","Training data shape: torch.Size([40000, 28, 28])\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The train set has data and targets given, yet test set has no targets. We have to train models based on the train data to achieve a high score on the leaderboard on the test set."],"metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.021709,"end_time":"2021-03-24T02:13:13.623869","exception":false,"start_time":"2021-03-24T02:13:13.60216","status":"completed"},"tags":[],"id":"VY5f2-D4nTnt"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Final Project: write an optimizer\n","\n","We will have 3 given CNN models as follows, and we will write our own optimizer(s) using `torch.optim` interface to optimize the given 3 models. You are free to use any techniques listed in the final project page to optimize the model. The goal is to optimize the model such that the model(s) trained performs good in the test set with unknown targets.\n","\n","## Models:\n","The 3 fixed models we can use are the famous first state-of-art image recognition CNN ResNet: ResNet 18, ResNet 34, and ResNet 50 [https://pytorch.org/hub/pytorch_vision_resnet/](https://pytorch.org/hub/pytorch_vision_resnet/). Their settings are in the next cell.\n","The `__init__()` has two parameters:\n","- `block`: the first type is the `BasicBlock` used for building ResNet, defined in the file (`torchvision.models.resnet`). The other type is `Bottleneck` block, which has a more agressive dimension reduction mechanics.\n","- `[2, 2, 2, 2]`: Each number denotes the number of `Bottleneck` or `BasicBlock` modules in a \"stage\". It depends on how deep you want the networks to be. For example, for ResNet18, it is `[2, 2, 2, 2]`; for ResNet34, it is `[3, 4, 6, 3]`.\n","\n","The full code of ResNet is here: [https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/master/torchvision/models/resnet.py](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/master/torchvision/models/resnet.py). We are just gonna import the `torchvision` implementation, and change the first convolutional layer to accept single channel input, and the stride of the first convolutional layer from 2 to 1.\n","\n","\n","## Validation:\n","In the first starter code, no validation technique is used. However for the final project, you are expected to use the validation technique featured in class to choose your best-performanced models.\n","\n","Since you do not have access to the target of the test set, to validate your model, you should split the training samples to two sets using the techniques learned in class: one is training dataset, the other is your validation dataset (so that you have access to the targets of this set). This routine is usually used for Kaggle competitions and in the real world model deployment to ensure the trained model has generalizability to the unseen data.\n","\n","## Hyperparameter tuning:\n","Aside from writing our own optimizer, there are quite a few hyperparameter for us to tune to achieve better performance:\n","- batch size\n","- learning rate and/or with a scheduler\n","- dropout rate\n","- early stop\n","- other validation strategy based tuning\n","It is okay to use autoML package (H2O, Rapids, Optuna, fast.ai) if you know how to write a wrapper of them using the given model."],"metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.020376,"end_time":"2021-03-24T02:13:15.391726","exception":false,"start_time":"2021-03-24T02:13:15.37135","status":"completed"},"tags":[],"id":"ke4imGc1nTnu"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from torchvision.models.resnet import ResNet, BasicBlock, Bottleneck\n","\n","class MyResNet(ResNet):\n","    def __init__(self,\n","                 block=BasicBlock,\n","                 layers=[2, 2, 2, 2],\n","                 num_classes=10):\n","        super(MyResNet, self).__init__(block,\n","                                       layers,\n","                                       num_classes=num_classes)\n","        self.conv1 = nn.Conv2d(1, 64, kernel_size=7, stride=1, padding=3,bias=False)\n","\n","        '''\n","        you can modify the layers in this initialization of ResNet if you like\n","        '''\n","\n","# choose 1\n","resnet18 = {\n","    \"block\": BasicBlock,\n","    \"layers\": [2, 2, 2, 2]\n","}\n","\n","resnet34 = {\n","    \"block\": BasicBlock,\n","    \"layers\": [3, 4, 6, 3]\n","}\n","\n","resnet50 = {\n","    \"block\": Bottleneck,\n","    \"layers\": [3, 4, 6, 3]\n","}\n","\n","\n","\n","model = MyResNet(**resnet18)"],"metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.398545,"end_time":"2021-03-24T02:13:15.810032","exception":false,"start_time":"2021-03-24T02:13:15.411487","status":"completed"},"tags":[],"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-11-13T21:35:32.306824Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-11-13T21:35:32.307517Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-11-13T21:35:35.880803Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-11-13T21:35:32.307495Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-11-13T21:35:35.880205Z"},"trusted":true,"id":"V7zcpATCnTnu","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1765949479364,"user_tz":360,"elapsed":6159,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"}}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"code","source":["!pip install torchinfo -q\n","from torchinfo import summary"],"metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":7.396057,"end_time":"2021-03-24T02:13:23.223496","exception":false,"start_time":"2021-03-24T02:13:15.827439","status":"completed"},"tags":[],"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-11-13T21:35:35.882148Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-11-13T21:35:35.882455Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-11-13T21:35:39.915184Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-11-13T21:35:35.882437Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-11-13T21:35:39.914431Z"},"trusted":true